P2 · WINDOWS · W7 — page:charging/ChargingHeatmap (WinUI 3 / Fluent)
====================================================================

Goal: native WinUI 3 / Windows App SDK / .NET 10 / Fluent parity port of the web
page ChargingHeatmapPage (web/src/features/charging/pages/ChargingHeatmapPage.tsx,
route /charging-heatmap, nav name ChargingHeatmap) at full panel / chart / state /
string parity. Delegation FORBIDDEN — implemented in this session. No placeholders
(ADR-011). SI read directly from the API; display-boundary scaling only.

Repo-convention note: the p2-windows feature surfaces are authored as C#-markup
UserControl views with a four-file split (.Model.cs / .Source.cs / .ViewModel.cs
/ .cs), NOT a hand-written .xaml + ViewModel pair. The manifest's hypothetical
output path apps/windows/TeslaSync/Features/Charging/ does not exist in this repo;
this port follows the actual sibling-page pattern (ChargingCurvePage,
ChargingDetailPage) verbatim: output dir
apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/ChargingHeatmapPage/, namespace
TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.Charging, nav registered in Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs.
The platform string catalog (Strings/en/Resources.resw) already carries all twelve
manifest keys (auto-generated from the web i18n), so no catalog edit was needed.

Honesty Covenant (binding): no red-as-green; no scope narrowing; no skip-and-assume;
no stubs as final; no parity shortcuts; no delegation; no predecessor bypass; no
commit on red; no silent drift; log ends with EXIT/STATUS.

